MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds express-rate-limit to the two credential-facing public endpoints:
- POST /api/v1/auth/login: 10 attempts / 15 min per IP (tighter, since
  this is the credential-stuffing/brute-force surface)
- POST /api/v1/auth/register: 5 attempts / hour per IP

Also sets 'trust proxy' in production so req.ip (and therefore the
rate-limit bucket) reflects the real client behind a load balancer
instead of everyone sharing one bucket.

Note: pre-existing repo hygiene issue found (not touched here) —
backend/node_modules/ is tracked in git despite .gitignore excluding
it; gitignore was added after node_modules was already committed.
Worth a follow-up cleanup (git rm -r --cached backend/node_modules).

Tests: 19/19 passing (added a rate-limit trip test).
